# FIXED DEFECT, 2026-08-12, sweep 001 audit S6. A carriage return that is not
# part of `\r\n` was swallowed unconditionally, under a comment saying "tolerated
# only as part of \\r\\n" — so `print(1)\rprint(2)` became two statements the
# compiler reported as being on one line, and the source line printed above the
# caret showed them merged, because a terminal eats the `\r` too. A tab gets a
# diagnostic; this got silence.
#
# One `\r` followed by a space rather than by a newline: the line still holds one
# statement, so the case is the stray return alone and not its cascade.

function main()
    print(1)  #~ stray_carriage_return
